From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:45:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bus: mhi: host: Separate mission-mode wait from startup
 teardown

mhi_sync_power_up() tears down MHI devices if startup fails. A driver
recovering across a PCIe reset needs to fence the transport first, so
it cannot use the synchronous API to wait for mission mode.

Extract the current wait into mhi_wait_for_mission_mode(), for use
after successful mhi_async_power_up(). Keep the normal synchronous
helper's error handling unchanged. The new wait does not stop
asynchronous state transitions.

The LLM implemented the extraction, checked the worker boundaries,
compiled ARM64 pm.o and tested both startup APIs on the host.

Link: https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux/+/1f7267d8043e394933b0ed06070bfa7921d7c830/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pm.c
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/bus/mhi/host/pm.c | 20 ++++++++++++++------
 include/linux/mhi.h       | 13 +++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pm.c b/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pm.c
index 702c12ba2..2a983bcb0 100644
--- a/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pm.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pm.c
@@ -1308,14 +1308,10 @@ void mhi_power_down_keep_dev(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl,
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mhi_power_down_keep_dev);
 
-int mhi_sync_power_up(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl)
+int mhi_wait_for_mission_mode(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl)
 {
-	int ret = mhi_async_power_up(mhi_cntrl);
 	u32 timeout_ms;
 
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
 	/* Some devices need more time to set ready during power up */
 	timeout_ms = mhi_cntrl->ready_timeout_ms ?
 		mhi_cntrl->ready_timeout_ms : mhi_cntrl->timeout_ms;
@@ -1324,7 +1320,19 @@ int mhi_sync_power_up(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl)
 			   MHI_PM_FATAL_ERROR(mhi_cntrl->pm_state),
 			   msecs_to_jiffies(timeout_ms));
 
-	ret = (MHI_IN_MISSION_MODE(mhi_cntrl->ee)) ? 0 : -ETIMEDOUT;
+	return MHI_IN_MISSION_MODE(mhi_cntrl->ee) ? 0 : -ETIMEDOUT;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mhi_wait_for_mission_mode);
+
+int mhi_sync_power_up(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = mhi_async_power_up(mhi_cntrl);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = mhi_wait_for_mission_mode(mhi_cntrl);
 	if (ret)
 		mhi_power_down(mhi_cntrl, false);
 
diff --git a/include/linux/mhi.h b/include/linux/mhi.h
index d26165660..bcb8fbd82 100644
--- a/include/linux/mhi.h
+++ b/include/linux/mhi.h
@@ -634,6 +634,19 @@ int mhi_prepare_for_power_up(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl);
  */
 int mhi_async_power_up(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl);
 
+/**
+ * mhi_wait_for_mission_mode - Wait for an asynchronous MHI startup
+ * @mhi_cntrl: MHI controller
+ *
+ * Call after mhi_async_power_up() succeeds. This function does not power down
+ * the controller or synchronize asynchronous work on failure. The controller
+ * driver remains responsible for quiescing the transport and shutting down
+ * MHI before releasing any DMA resources.
+ *
+ * Return: 0 if the device reaches mission mode, or -ETIMEDOUT otherwise.
+ */
+int mhi_wait_for_mission_mode(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl);
+
 /**
  * mhi_sync_power_up - Start MHI power up sequence and wait till the device
  *                     enters valid EE state
